<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>AccountabilityGap on behaviorengineering.ai</title><link>https://behaviorengineering.ai/pr-preview/pr-40/tags/accountabilitygap/</link><description>Recent content in AccountabilityGap on behaviorengineering.ai</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Sun, 04 Oct 2026 01:00:00 +1100</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://behaviorengineering.ai/pr-preview/pr-40/tags/accountabilitygap/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Stable Enough to Remain Unpredictable</title><link>https://behaviorengineering.ai/pr-preview/pr-40/cognitive-memetics/reptilocracy/2026-10-04-stable-enough-to-remain-unpredictable/</link><pubDate>Sun, 04 Oct 2026 01:00:00 +1100</pubDate><guid>https://behaviorengineering.ai/pr-preview/pr-40/cognitive-memetics/reptilocracy/2026-10-04-stable-enough-to-remain-unpredictable/</guid><description/></item><item><title>🔄 How bystanders learn to sustain a blamer</title><link>https://behaviorengineering.ai/pr-preview/pr-40/social-protocols/2026-09-29-the-mirror-that-only-blames/</link><pubDate>Tue, 29 Sep 2026 01:00:00 +1100</pubDate><guid>https://behaviorengineering.ai/pr-preview/pr-40/social-protocols/2026-09-29-the-mirror-that-only-blames/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;A vampire checks the mirror after a feeding. The glass stays empty. Without a reflection to show the blood or the hunger, the vampire looks around for the source of the mess. The blank surface directs the fault toward the furniture, the lighting, or the people standing nearby.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This &lt;strong&gt;blindness functions as a closed circuit&lt;/strong&gt;. When a person cannot register their own image, they &lt;strong&gt;lose the ability to locate fault within themselves&lt;/strong&gt;. They search for a problem and find only a &lt;strong&gt;void where accountability should live&lt;/strong&gt;. This void &lt;strong&gt;pushes blame outward&lt;/strong&gt;. Every mistake becomes a problem caused by the environment or the people in it. &lt;strong&gt;Everyone nearby becomes a target&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>The Bridge Is Open</title><link>https://behaviorengineering.ai/pr-preview/pr-40/cognitive-memetics/reptilocracy/2026-09-27-the-bridge-is-open/</link><pubDate>Sun, 27 Sep 2026 01:00:00 +1100</pubDate><guid>https://behaviorengineering.ai/pr-preview/pr-40/cognitive-memetics/reptilocracy/2026-09-27-the-bridge-is-open/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Good Days, Bad Days</title><link>https://behaviorengineering.ai/pr-preview/pr-40/cognitive-memetics/reptilocracy/2026-09-20-good-days-bad-days/</link><pubDate>Sun, 20 Sep 2026 01:00:00 +1100</pubDate><guid>https://behaviorengineering.ai/pr-preview/pr-40/cognitive-memetics/reptilocracy/2026-09-20-good-days-bad-days/</guid><description/></item><item><title>The Alarm Worked</title><link>https://behaviorengineering.ai/pr-preview/pr-40/cognitive-memetics/reptilocracy/2026-09-13-the-alarm-worked/</link><pubDate>Sun, 13 Sep 2026 01:00:00 +1100</pubDate><guid>https://behaviorengineering.ai/pr-preview/pr-40/cognitive-memetics/reptilocracy/2026-09-13-the-alarm-worked/</guid><description/></item><item><title>The Self-Certified Certificate</title><link>https://behaviorengineering.ai/pr-preview/pr-40/cognitive-memetics/reptilocracy/2026-09-06-the-self-certified-certificate/</link><pubDate>Sun, 06 Sep 2026 01:00:00 +1100</pubDate><guid>https://behaviorengineering.ai/pr-preview/pr-40/cognitive-memetics/reptilocracy/2026-09-06-the-self-certified-certificate/</guid><descr